        <section class="legal-page__content">

            <div class="container">

                <article class="legal-page__article">

                    <p class="legal-page__updated">
                        Last updated: August 2026
                    </p>


                    <h2>
                        Introduction
                    </h2>

                    <p>
                        Welcome to ToolZen Hub. This Privacy Policy
                        explains how information may be collected,
                        used, and protected when you use our website
                        and services.
                    </p>


                    <h2>
                        Information We Collect
                    </h2>

                    <p>
                        ToolZen Hub may collect information that you
                        voluntarily provide, such as information
                        you send us when you contact us.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        We may also collect basic technical information
                        required to operate, maintain, and improve the
                        website.
                    </p>


                    <h2>
                        How We Use Information
                    </h2>

                    <p>
                        Information may be used to provide and improve
                        our services, respond to inquiries, maintain
                        website functionality, and communicate with
                        users when appropriate.
                    </p>


                    <h2>
                        Cookies and Analytics
                    </h2>

                    <p>
                        The calculators and tools run in your browser.
                        What you type into them, and any file you
                        choose, stays on your device and is not sent to
                        us or to Google.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        On toolzenhub.in we would like to use Google
                        Analytics 4 to count visits and see which pages
                        are useful. Google Analytics uses cookies and
                        sends page and device information, such as the
                        page address (without any query string), your
                        approximate location, and your browser and
                        device type, to Google. It stays switched off
                        until you press &ldquo;Accept analytics&rdquo;
                        in the notice shown on the site. If you press
                        &ldquo;Reject analytics&rdquo;, Google Analytics
                        is not loaded and no analytics cookies are set.
                        Your choice is remembered in your browser&rsquo;s
                        local storage, and you can change it at any
                        time.
                    </p>
{%- if site.analyticsId %}

                    <p>
                        <span data-tz-analytics-status>Analytics: no choice made yet.</span>
                        <button type="button" class="tz-consent__btn" data-tz-analytics-settings>
                            Change analytics choice
                        </button>
                    </p>
{%- endif %}


                    <h2>
                        Third-Party Services
                    </h2>

                    <p>
                        Some website features may rely on third-party
                        services. Those services may have their own
                        privacy policies and terms.
                    </p>

                    <p>
                        Some pages show article pictures that are loaded
                        from a third-party image host (currently
                        Unsplash). Opening such a page makes your browser
                        request those pictures, so that host can see
                        your IP address and browser details, as with any
                        web image. This is separate from the calculators,
                        which do not send what you type to anyone, and it
                        happens whatever you choose about analytics.
                    </p>


                    <h2>
                        Data Security
                    </h2>

                    <p>
                        We take reasonable steps to protect information
                        associated with the website. However, no method
                        of transmission or storage can be guaranteed to
                        be completely secure.
                    </p>


                    <h2>
                        Changes to This Policy
                    </h2>

                    <p>
                        This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to
                        time. Changes will be reflected on this page.
                    </p>


                    <h2>
                        Contact Us
                    </h2>

                    <p>
                        If you have questions about this Privacy Policy,
                        please visit our
                        <a href="{{ '/contact.html' | url }}">
                            Contact Us
                        </a>
                        page.
                    </p>

